---
description: Enforce cohesive delivery and prevent lifecycle or bookkeeping loops
alwaysApply: true
---

# Real progress

- One PR represents a meaningful cohesive vertical slice with implementation,
  tests, documentation, traceability, generated artifacts, and rollback as needed.
- Never create a PR whose only product effect is a lifecycle transition, snapshot,
  manifest refresh, Jira projection, evidence rewrite, or generated-index update.
- Never disguise lifecycle-only work with unrelated source, test, config, or docs edits.
- Batch compatible already-implemented/evidenced reconciliation.
- Run expensive gates once at the cohesive slice boundary, not at each lifecycle label.
- The default maximum is two conflict-safe implementation lanes.
- After two consecutive cycles without accepted implementation, blocker reduction,
  valid new evidence, corrected diagnosis, integration, or exact escalation, stop
  selection and repair the planner/model before continuing.
- Do not rerun an unchanged failing strategy beyond the canonical attempt budget.
